      "body": "### Motivation\n\n`BlockedAllocator.free()` validates every block for validity *before* mutating the free list, but the \"already free\" check cannot detect duplicates **within a single call**: marking happens in the second (mutation) loop, so both passes see the stale `-1` marker for a repeated id.\n\nRepro (pure CPU, no model or GPU needed):\n\n```python\nallocator = BlockedAllocator(4)\na = allocator.allocate(3)      # blocks [0, 1, 2]\nallocator.free([0, 0, 1])      # passes validation\n# free_blocks is now 4 (should be 2): block 0 is in the free list twice\nb = allocator.allocate(2)      # returns [1, 0]\n# block 0 is handed out while sequence 1 still owns it -> two sequences\n# share one KV block and silently overwrite each other's cache state\n```\n\nThe same call path is reachable from production code: `DSStateManager.flush_sequence()` passes `seq.all_block_ids()` (a Tensor) into `BlockedKVCache.free()` -> `BlockedAllocator.free()`. Iterating that Tensor yields 0-dim tensors, which hash by identity -- so even a set-based duplicate check would be defeated without normalizing to `int`.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. In the validation pass, reject ids that appear more than once in the same `free()` call (`Block X provided multiple times to free`).\n2. Normalize each element with `int(block)` before checking, so Tensor inputs go through the same code path.\n\nNo behavior change for valid inputs: the free-list mutation loop is untouched.\n\n### Tests\n\nAdded `test_free_duplicate_block_rejected` in `tests/unit/inference/v2/ragged/test_blocked_allocator.py`:\n\n- duplicate `free()` raises `ValueError`\n- allocator state is unchanged by the failed call (`free_blocks` stays consistent)\n- the blocks can still be freed exactly once afterwards, and a full allocate/free cycle yields no duplicate ids\n\n### Test commands / results\n\n- Pre-fix repro on CPU (pin_memory shim): `free([0, 0, 1])` succeeded and a subsequent `allocate(2)` returned `[1, 0]` -- block 0 allocated twice.\n- Post-fix: the duplicate call raises `ValueError: Block 0 provided multiple times to free`; `free_blocks` stays consistent.\n- `flake8` on changed files: clean.\n- No GPU was required for this change: the allocator is host-side pure-Python logic; the added test runs under the existing `inference_v2` marker and only needs `BlockedAllocator` construction (CPU with pinned-memory shim locally; will exercise natively on the GPU CI runners).\n\n### Duplicate check\n\nSearched issues and PRs for `BlockedAllocator`, \"already free\", \"allocated twice\", \"duplicate block\" (both deepspeedai/DeepSpeed and legacy microsoft/DeepSpeed) -- no existing report. PR #8503 (fixing #5407) touches only `engine_v2.py` and does not include this fix.\n\n### AI assistance\n\nThis fix was prepared with AI coding assistance; the submitting human has reviewed every changed line and the verification above.\n\nSigned-off-by: likehong <likehong@kingsoft.com>",
